  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "InverseBlitter::prepost",
    "file": "skia/src/core/SkScan_Path.cpp",
    "description": "Integer overflow in inverse-span bookkeeping leads to negative/invalid X passed to blitter. In InverseBlitter::prepost(), fPrevX is set from shifted clip coordinates (clip.fLeft<<shift), and later invWidth=fLastX-fPrevX is computed in int without overflow checks. With fuzzed path/clip state, fPrevX can become very large/negative via x+width in InverseBlitter::blitH(), so prepost() calls fBlitter->blitH(fPrevX,y,invWidth) with out-of-bounds coordinates. This propagates through SkRectClipBlitter/SkARGB32_Blitter into SkBlitRow::Color32, where SIMD Load reads from an invalid src pointer and crashes.",
    "conditions": "Triggered via api_raster_n32_canvas when drawing an inverse-filled path. Fuzzed commands create extreme geometry/edge values so InverseBlitter receives spans with pathological x/width; fPrevX update (x+width) and later invWidth subtraction overflow/wrap. The resulting invalid left/width are forwarded to SkARGB32_Blitter::blitH(), which obtains device pointers using those coordinates and calls SkBlitRow::Color32(device,device,width,...). In optimized blit_row_color32(), vector Load(src) dereferences wild memory, causing the ASan SEGV."
  },
